Z||000000||theogre||08-06-2001||07:50 PM||||If you can still find these in a store near you, grab them. They have been discontinued. I got one on clearance at Kmart. I'll check other stores in the area over the next few days. <P>They are worth the full price if that's what they are marked. You get year specific stuff that was left out of Haynes/Chilton. <P>These are the only decent source of information for 87-88 4 cylinder cars other than a Helm shop book. (Some data on the CD is actually supliments the Helm book.) It has all the stuff left out of Haynes, like the V5 AC setup, DIS ECM and wiring, Type 2 headlight wiring, etc.<P>The replacement to the CD is a subscrition to ALLDATA DIY for $24.95 a year.<P>The CD and the online service provide the same data as ALLdata pro products. You just have a 1 car license.<P>You register year make and model of the car. you can then view the library for any engine option it had. In fiero that means you can read both the V6 and L4 libraries.<P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Songman||08-06-2001||08:41 PM||||I'm lucky.. my friend has the full AllData set with upgrades and support at his shop. And it's only 10 minutes from my house! I have used it lots of times!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
