Z||000003||PAUL88GT||08-08-2001||03:41 PM||||Ogre:<BR>Does the ALLDATA CD have the GM part numbers that are in the 22P Manual? <BR>Thanks<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-08-2001||07:10 PM||||No. Some TSB's have part numbers in them but that's about it. <P>The CD has the complete set of wire diagrams for each year and motor. something lacking in haynes/chilton. Has allot of other year specific data as well.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Posthumane||08-08-2001||09:35 PM||||I had alldata access at my school, and i was quite disappointed with it. It was missing alot of info, and some of the info it had was incorrect. (eg, fiero isn't an F body)||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-09-2001||08:00 PM||||Nearly all fiero data sources contian errors. Did you ever actually read the Haynes or Chilton books? <P>Haynes is all messed up. It doesn't cover DIS or much of anything else for the 87-88 4 cyl cars.<P>ALLDATA was never intended to be a complete reference. It was built up for profesionals that should know allot of the basic things. It's biggest uses area AC and TSB information along with the wiring diagrams for neary every item in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Posthumane||08-09-2001||08:24 PM||||Yeah, I guess that's true. It just seemed a little lacking for what it claimed. I had problems with it for other cars too, not just fieros. It was good for the electrical info, but for other stuff, i really prefered the shop manuals that it was supposed to replace.||||reg||1
